# Old URLs kept alive after the GROUNDINGS -> INQUIRIES rename.
#
# No grounding was ever published, so the only address anyone can hold is the
# section page itself — but that one was live, was in the sitemap, and is still
# sitting in Cloudflare's edge cache serving a page for a register that no
# longer exists. A redirect is what turns a dead end into an arrival, and it
# costs nothing to keep.
#
# 301, not 302: the rename is permanent, and a permanent redirect is what
# consolidates accumulated links onto the real address rather than asking every
# client to re-check forever. Same reasoning as the pages.dev hop in
# functions/_middleware.js.
#
# The splat covers the part URLs that would have existed had anything shipped
# under the old register, so a link written from the old PUBLISHING.md still
# lands somewhere useful rather than on a 404.
/groundings     /inquiries/   301
/groundings/    /inquiries/   301
/groundings/*   /inquiries/   301
